        "description": "LEVELS §2.2 — four places, spawn to gate. The Dock: a walled alcove on the west edge whose mouth is a broken gate frame, so the player enters the game through a door that no longer closes. Mid-edge rather than a corner on purpose: spawn positions clamp into the arena, and a corner spawn pulls clamped arrivals visibly close. The Stacks: rows of long slabs, server-rack rhythm, weaving lanes. The Spill: open kill-floor around one broken quarantine ring, the room's landmark. The Forecourt: the approach thins, the seal light carries, two flanking blocks give the siege something to be fought around. Motes and Drifters and nothing else — no Suppressor; a mechanic that reads as the game being broken is the worst possible first lesson. The gate siege introduces one, arriving with The Sink's roster: the room you are about to enter, showing you what it has. Threat 5 arrives inside three minutes and the room visibly stops escalating, which is the level itself saying move on. The run's Threat keeps climbing behind the door.",
        "light": 10473727
      },
